(Big-Endian using pointers and bitwise access, \(2\) Count total set bits \(1s\) in a 32-bit) Tj
T*
(integer using Brian Kernighan's algorithm.) Tj
T*
(Source Code:) Tj
T*
(#include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(int countSetBits\(unsigned int n\) {) Tj
T*
(int count = 0;) Tj
T*
(while \(n > 0\) {) Tj
T*
(n = n & \(n - 1\); /* Clears lowest set bit in O\(k\) iterations */) Tj
T*
(count++;) Tj
T*
(}) Tj
T*
(return count;) Tj
T*
(}) Tj
T*
(int main\(\) {) Tj
T*
(unsigned int x = 1;) Tj
T*
(char *c = \(char*\)&x;) Tj
T*
(if \(*c == 1\)) Tj
T*
(printf\("Architecture: Little-Endian \(LSB stored first\)\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(else) Tj
T*
(printf\("Architecture: Big-Endian \(MSB stored first\)\\n"\);) Tj
T*
(unsigned int val = 29;) Tj
T*
(printf\("Integer: %u | Set Bits Count: %d\\n", val, countSetBits\(val\)\);) Tj
T*
(return 0;) Tj
T*
(}) Tj
T*
(Algorithm Trace for val = 29 \(Binary 11101\):) Tj
T*
(Iteration 1: n = 29 \(11101\) & 28 \(11100\) = 28. count = 1.) Tj
T*
(Iteration 2: n = 28 \(11100\) & 27 \(11011\) = 24. count = 2.) Tj
T*
(Iteration 3: n = 24 \(11000\) & 23 \(10111\) = 16. count = 3.) Tj
T*
(Iteration 4: n = 16 \(10000\) & 15 \(01111\) = 0. count = 4. Terminate.) Tj
T*
(Output: Architecture: Little-Endian | Set Bits Count: 4.) Tj
