(* Q1: Explain the four stages of the C compilation system in detail, naming the) Tj
T*
(intermediate files produced.) Tj
T*
(Answer: The compilation system transforms source code \(prog.c\) into machine executable) Tj
T*
(through four stages: \(1\) Preprocessing \(cpp\): Executes all directives beginning with) Tj
T*
('#'. Replaces #include header lines with literal text of header files, replaces #define) Tj
T*
(macros with replacement strings, and strips comments. Produces expanded preprocessed) Tj
T*
(source file \(prog.i\). \(2\) Compilation \(c1\): Analyzes syntax, builds abstract syntax) Tj
T*
(trees, and optimizes code, translating high-level C code into target-specific assembly) Tj
T*
(code \(prog.s\). \(3\) Assembly \(as\): Translates assembly mnemonics into machine code) Tj
T*
(instructions, packaging them into relocatable object format \(prog.o\). \(4\) Linking \(ld\):) Tj
T*
(Resolves external references, connects runtime startup code, and links standard C) Tj
T*
(library functions \(e.g., printf in libc\), generating final executable binary \(prog.exe) Tj
T*
(or a.out\).) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Differentiate between implicit type conversion \(type promotion\) and explicit) Tj
T*
(type casting in C with examples.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Implicit conversion is performed automatically by the compiler when operands of) Tj
T*
(mixed types appear in an expression. The smaller type is promoted following standard) Tj
T*
(conversion hierarchy: char/short -> int -> unsigned int -> long -> float -> double ->) Tj
T*
(long double. Example: in 'int i = 5; float f = 2.5; float res = i + f;', i is promoted) Tj
T*
(to float \(5.0f\). Explicit casting is performed intentionally by the programmer using) Tj
T*
('\(target_type\)expression'. Example: 'int a = 5, b = 2; double d = \(double\)a / b;') Tj
T*
(explicitly casts 'a' to double \(5.0\), forcing floating-point division to yield 2.5) Tj
T*
(instead of integer truncation 2.) Tj
T*
